{%- comment -%}
  Reusable, server-rendered rail for informational and low-stock pages.

  Inputs:
    heading       visible heading
    intro         short supporting copy
    placement     analytics placement/list name
    limit         maximum cards (default 4)
    one_only      when true, require total inventory == 1
    min_price     optional price floor in cents
    max_price     optional price ceiling in cents
    exclude_ids   comma-wrapped product ids, e.g. ",123,456,"
    compact       two-column compact layout for a PDP buy panel
    prefer_collection  a collection object whose in-stock products are offered FIRST
    prefer_vendor      a vendor name used as the second-choice tier

  RELEVANCE TIERS (added 2026-08-29)
    Until this change the pool was `collections.all.products | where: 'available'`
    with no relevance filter at all — not collection, not type, not vendor. On a
    sold-out PDP that meant the "شوف البدائل" rail offered whatever the store
    happened to list first.

    Measured on the live storefront 2026-08-29: the sold-out
    adidas-black-3-stripes-track-pants PDP holds 83 impressions for
    «بنطال تراك أسود للرجال» (pos 9–18) and offered football boots, three pairs of
    shorts and a crossbody bag — while FOUR in-stock black track pants sat in the
    same collection (two Nike joggers at 349, a Jordan at 599, an Adidas at 499).
    Someone searching for black track pants was shown a bag.

    Order is now: same collection → same vendor → store-wide. The store-wide tier
    is kept as the last resort so the rail can never render empty, which is the
    behaviour every other caller of this snippet relies on.

  Only available products render. No product or condition claim is invented:
  the condition label appears only when the inspection metafield confirms it.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign lr_heading = heading | default: 'قطع متوفرة دابا'
  assign lr_intro = intro | default: 'صور حقيقية، القياس والحالة واضحين، والمخزون كيتحدث من Shopify.'
  assign lr_placement = placement | default: 'live_products'
  assign lr_limit = limit | default: 4
  assign lr_exclude = exclude_ids | default: ','

  comment
    Build the pool in relevance tiers, then concatenate. `concat` needs arrays,
    so every tier is filtered with `where` (which returns an array) rather than
    built by hand. Duplicates across tiers are harmless: the card loop already
    skips a product it has drawn once via lr_exclude, and the same guard is
    extended below to cover repeats.
  endcomment
  assign lr_pool = ''
  assign lr_all = collections.all.products | where: 'available', true

  comment
    TYPE is the first tier, not collection. Measured 2026-08-29: for the sold-out
    adidas-black-3-stripes-track-pants PDP, product.liquid's `first_collection`
    resolves to adidas-originals (it takes the first non-brand- collection in
    product.collections order), NOT track-pants — so a collection-first pool
    returned Adidas shorts. Type answers "same kind of thing" directly and
    survives a product sitting in several collections.

    Use `type`, not `product_type`: product_type reads empty from
    collections[].products on this storefront (see the Adidas snippet block in
    layout/theme.liquid for the same trap).
  endcomment
  comment
    Tier 0 is type AND vendor — the closest possible substitute. Type alone put
    H&M grey cargo pants ahead of an in-stock black Adidas track pant for a
    shopper who searched «بنطال تراك أسود للرجال»: right category, wrong answer.
  endcomment
  if prefer_type != blank and prefer_vendor != blank
    assign lr_tier0 = lr_all | where: 'type', prefer_type | where: 'vendor', prefer_vendor
    assign lr_pool = lr_tier0
  endif

  if prefer_type != blank
    assign lr_tier1 = lr_all | where: 'type', prefer_type
    if lr_pool == ''
      assign lr_pool = lr_tier1
    else
      assign lr_pool = lr_pool | concat: lr_tier1
    endif
  endif

  if prefer_collection != blank and prefer_collection.products.size > 0
    assign lr_tier2 = prefer_collection.products | where: 'available', true
    if lr_pool == ''
      assign lr_pool = lr_tier2
    else
      assign lr_pool = lr_pool | concat: lr_tier2
    endif
  endif

  if prefer_vendor != blank
    assign lr_tier3 = lr_all | where: 'vendor', prefer_vendor
    if lr_pool == ''
      assign lr_pool = lr_tier3
    else
      assign lr_pool = lr_pool | concat: lr_tier3
    endif
  endif

  if lr_pool == ''
    assign lr_pool = lr_all
  else
    assign lr_pool = lr_pool | concat: lr_all
  endif
  assign lr_count = 0
  assign lr_one_only_count = 0
  if one_only
    for lr_candidate in lr_pool
      if lr_candidate.total_inventory == 1
        assign lr_one_only_count = lr_one_only_count | plus: 1
      endif
      if lr_one_only_count >= lr_limit
        break
      endif
    endfor
    if lr_one_only_count == 0
      assign lr_heading = 'قطع مختارة متوفرة دابا'
      assign lr_intro = 'المخزون كيتبدل بسرعة. هادو قطع متوفرة دابا بصورها الحقيقية، القياس والحالة واضحين قبل الطلب.'
    endif
  endif
-%}

{%- capture lr_cards -%}
  {%- for lr_product in lr_pool -%}
    {%- if lr_count >= lr_limit -%}{%- break -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- capture lr_pid -%},{{ lr_product.id }},{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- if lr_exclude contains lr_pid -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- if one_only and lr_one_only_count > 0 and lr_product.total_inventory != 1 -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- if min_price != blank and lr_product.price < min_price -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- if max_price != blank and lr_product.price > max_price -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}

    {%- liquid
      assign lr_variant = lr_product.selected_or_first_available_variant
      assign lr_title = lr_product.title | split: ' — LBO-' | first | split: ' - LBO-' | first | split: ' – LBO-' | first | split: ' — ' | first
      assign lr_status = lr_product.metafields.lbass.condition_status.value | default: 'unknown'
      assign lr_inspection = lr_product.metafields.lbass.inspection_status.value
      assign lr_ticket = lr_product.metafields.lbass.ticket_status.value | default: 'unknown'
      assign lr_has_ticket = lr_product.metafields.lbass.has_original_ticket.value
      assign lr_notes = lr_product.metafields.lbass.condition_notes.value
      assign lr_defects = lr_product.metafields.lbass.visible_defects.value
      assign lr_condition = ''
      if lr_inspection == 'inspected_confirmed'
        if lr_has_ticket == true and lr_status == 'new_with_ticket'
          if lr_ticket == 'ticket_attached' or lr_ticket == 'ticket_included'
            assign lr_condition = 'جديد بالتّيكيت'
          endif
        elsif lr_has_ticket == false and lr_ticket == 'no_ticket' and lr_status == 'new_without_ticket'
          assign lr_condition = 'جديد بلا تيكيت'
        elsif lr_has_ticket == false and lr_ticket == 'no_ticket' and lr_status == 'excellent_almost_new'
          assign lr_condition = 'بحالة ممتازة · شبه جديد'
        elsif lr_status == 'very_good'
          assign lr_condition = 'بحالة مزيانة بزاف'
        elsif lr_status == 'good'
          assign lr_condition = 'بحالة مزيانة'
        elsif lr_status == 'needs_note'
          if lr_notes != blank or lr_defects != blank
            assign lr_condition = 'شوف ملاحظات الحالة'
          endif
        endif
      endif
      comment
        Tiered pools can list the same product twice (collection tier and
        store-wide tier). Adding each drawn id to lr_exclude reuses the guard
        that already runs at the top of this loop, so a repeat is skipped
        instead of rendering a duplicate card.
      endcomment
      assign lr_exclude = lr_exclude | append: lr_product.id | append: ','
      assign lr_count = lr_count | plus: 1
    -%}

    <div class="lblr-card-wrap">
      <a class="lblr-card"
         href="{{ lr_product.url }}"
         data-cro-product-card
         data-cro-placement="{{ lr_placement | escape }}"
         data-product-id="{{ lr_product.id }}"
         data-product-name="{{ lr_title | escape }}"
         data-product-handle="{{ lr_product.handle | escape }}">
        <span class="lblr-media">
          {%- if lr_product.featured_image -%}
            <img src="{{ lr_product.featured_image | image_url: width: 640 }}"
                 alt="{{ lr_product.featured_image.alt | default: lr_title | escape }}"
                 loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="640" height="800">
          {%- else -%}
            <span class="lblr-no-image">{{ lr_product.vendor | escape }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
          <span class="lblr-live">متوفرة دابا</span>
        </span>
        <span class="lblr-body">
          <span class="lblr-brand">{{ lr_product.vendor | escape }}</span>
          <strong class="lblr-title" dir="auto">{{ lr_title }}</strong>
          <span class="lblr-row">
            <b>{{ lr_variant.price | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</b>
            {%- unless lr_variant.title == 'Default Title' -%}<span>{{ lr_variant.title }}</span>{%- endunless -%}
          </span>
          {%- if lr_condition != blank -%}<span class="lblr-condition">{{ lr_condition }}</span>{%- endif -%}
        </span>
      </a>
      {% render 'lbass-quick-add', product: lr_product %}
    </div>
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- if lr_count > 0 -%}
<section class="lblr{% if compact %} lblr--compact{% endif %}"
         aria-labelledby="lblr-{{ lr_placement | handleize }}-h"
         data-cro-list
         data-cro-list-name="{{ lr_placement | escape }}">
  <div class="lblr-head">
    <div>
      <p class="lblr-kicker">AVAILABLE NOW</p>
      <h2 id="lblr-{{ lr_placement | handleize }}-h">{{ lr_heading }}</h2>
      <p>{{ lr_intro }}</p>
    </div>
    <a href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}"
       data-cro-event="available_now_click"
       data-cro-label="{{ lr_placement | escape }}"
       data-source-section="{{ lr_placement | escape }}">شوف الكل →</a>
  </div>
  <div class="lblr-grid" role="list">{{ lr_cards }}</div>
</section>

<style>
.lblr{max-width:1100px;margin:24px 0;padding:20px;border:1px solid rgba(200,154,14,.28);border-radius:16px;background:rgba(200,154,14,.055)}
.lblr-head{display:flex;align-items:end;justify-content:space-between;gap:18px;margin:0 0 16px}
.lblr-kicker{margin:0 0 5px!important;color:var(--gold,#c89a0e)!important;font:800 10px/1.2 ui-monospace,monospace!important;letter-spacing:.18em!important;direction:ltr}
.lblr-head h2{margin:0 0 5px!important;color:var(--cream,#F4EFE6)!important;font-size:clamp(20px,2.5vw,28px)!important;line-height:1.35!important}
.lblr-head p:not(.lblr-kicker){margin:0!important;color:var(--txt2,#97928A)!important;font-size:13px!important;line-height:1.7!important}
.lblr-head>a{flex:none;color:var(--gold2,#E0B52A);font-size:13px;font-weight:900;text-decoration:none}
.lblr-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));gap:12px}
.lblr-card-wrap{min-width:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;border:1px solid var(--line,rgba(255,255,255,.12));border-radius:13px;background:var(--ink2,#151518);overflow:hidden}
.lblr-card{display:flex;flex:1;flex-direction:column;color:inherit;text-decoration:none;min-width:0}
.lblr-media{display:block;position:relative;aspect-ratio:4/5;overflow:hidden;background:#171719}
.lblr-media img{width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;display:block;transition:transform .25s ease}
.lblr-card:hover .lblr-media img{transform:scale(1.025)}
.lblr-live{position:absolute;top:9px;right:9px;padding:5px 8px;border-radius:999px;background:#176d3a;color:#fff;font-size:10px;font-weight:900}
.lblr-no-image{height:100%;display:grid;place-items:center;color:#fff;font-weight:900}
.lblr-body{display:flex;flex:1;flex-direction:column;padding:12px}
.lblr-brand{color:var(--gold,#c89a0e);font-size:10px;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;direction:ltr}
.lblr-title{display:block;margin:5px 0 9px;color:var(--cream,#F4EFE6);font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.45}
.lblr-row{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:8px;margin-top:auto;color:var(--cream,#F4EFE6);font-size:12px;direction:ltr}
.lblr-row b{font-size:14px;color:var(--gold2,#E0B52A)}
.lblr-condition{display:block;margin-top:7px;color:var(--txt2,#97928A);font-size:10.5px;line-height:1.4}
.lblr .lbqa-btn{margin:0 10px 10px}
.lblr--compact{margin:12px 0;padding:13px}
.lblr--compact .lblr-head{align-items:start;margin-bottom:11px}
.lblr--compact .lblr-head h2{font-size:16px!important}
.lblr--compact .lblr-head p:not(.lblr-kicker){display:none}
.lblr--compact .lblr-grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:8px}
.lblr--compact .lblr-title{font-size:11.5px}.lblr--compact .lblr-condition{display:none}
.lblr--compact .lblr-body{padding:9px}.lblr--compact .lbqa-btn{font-size:11px!important;margin:0 7px 7px!important;padding:8px!important;min-height:38px!important}
@media(max-width:780px){.lblr-grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}}
@media(max-width:520px){.lblr{padding:14px;margin:18px 0}.lblr-head{align-items:start}.lblr-head>a{font-size:12px}.lblr-grid{gap:9px}.lblr-title{font-size:12px}}
</style>
{%- endif -%}
